### **5. How much does therapy cost with insurance?**

The cost depends on your insurance plan, deductible, copayment, coinsurance, and whether the therapist is in-network.

Some plans have a fixed copayment for each appointment, while others require members to pay toward their deductible before insurance contributes.

Contact your insurance company or counseling practice for an estimate based on your specific benefits.

### **6. Can I use insurance for online therapy in Texas?**

Many health insurance plans cover eligible outpatient mental health services through telehealth. However, coverage depends on the specific plan, provider, service, and applicable requirements.

Check whether your insurance covers virtual counseling and whether your therapist is eligible to provide telehealth services under your plan.

### **7. Do I need a referral to see a therapist?**

Not always. Some insurance plans allow members to schedule directly with an in-network mental health professional, while others may have referral or authorization requirements.

Check your policy or contact your insurance company before scheduling your first appointment.

### **8. What if my insurance does not cover the therapist I want?**

You may still have options.

Ask the counseling practice whether it offers self-pay appointments, reduced-fee options, or other arrangements. You can also check whether your insurance provides out-of-network reimbursement.

Review the expected costs before beginning treatment so you can choose an option that fits your financial situation.

